  <!--
    x64 only. A build is a "base" plus two independent, additive flavor macros:
      EMOT3_PLUS     - the +plus flavor: the input-SWALLOW conveniences
                       (QuickbarWheel + SendSuppress + the plus.json toggles).
                       They consume input in the WndProc (AV-sensitive), so the
                       base build leaves them out. Code lives in src/plus/.
      EMOT3_DEVTOOLS - the +devtools flavor: the diagnostic dev TOOLS (perf
                       overlay, QB sizing readout, runtime state inspector,
                       notifier / update-check testers). Code lives in src/devtools/.
                       (Both flavor folders are on the include path; includes
                       stay flat - see AdditionalIncludeDirectories.)
    base = neither macro = the public build.

    Five configurations (-> output DLL):
      Distribution  - base. Optimized. No swallows, no dev tools. The shipped
                      public build (CI publishes).               -> emot3.dll
      Plus          - base +plus. Swallow conveniences on, no dev tools. The
                      power-user convenience build.              -> emot3_plus.dll
      DevTools      - base +devtools. Dev tools on, no swallows - diagnose a
                      base-shaped binary.                    -> emot3_devtools.dll
      PlusDevTools  - base +plus +devtools. Swallows + dev tools. The local
                      diagnostic build.                  -> emot3_plusdevtools.dll
      Debug         - +plus +devtools, unoptimized + debug CRT, for stepping.
                                                                -> emot3_debug.dll
    Each configuration writes to its own folder under build\ (see OutDir/IntDir
    below) so builds never clobber each other and incremental state survives
    config switches. TargetName is per-config so the DLLs don't collide.
  -->
